reasoning_details.text:
Now let's build a probe to measure layout with headless Chrome. I'll create a temp file in the task dir (allowed) that imports the same page via iframe? Simpler: create `_probe.html` that is a copy of index.html with an appended script that measures and dumps results into the DOM, then use `--dump-dom`. Then delete probe file.

Measurement script:
```js
window.addEventListener('load', function(){
 setTimeout(function(){
  const r = el => { const b = el.getBoundingClientRect(); return {x:+b.x.toFixed(1),y:+b.y.toFixed(1),w:+b.width.toFixed(1),h:+b.height.toFixed(1),r:+b.right.toFixed(1),b:+b.bottom.toFixed(1)}; };
  const q = s => document.querySelector(s);
  const out = {
    vw: innerWidth, scrollW: document.documentElement.scrollWidth,
    bodyScrollW: document.body.scrollWidth,
    overflowX: document.documentElement.scrollWidth > innerWidth,
    display: r(q('.display')), line2: r(q('.display__line--2')), wl: r(q('.waterline')),
    wlTickL: r(q('.waterline__tick--l')), wlTickR: r(q('.waterline__tick--r')),
    aside: r(q('.hero__aside')),
    wrap: r(q('.hero .wrap')),
    motif: r(q('.motif__svg')),
    capHi: r(q('.motif__cap--hi')),
    done: getComputedStyle(q('#signup-done')).display,
    err: getComputedStyle(q('#email-error')).display,
    navDisplay: getComputedStyle(q('.masthead__nav')).display,
    headH: r(q('.masthead')).h,
  };
  // overflow offenders
  out.offenders = [...document.querySelectorAll('body *')].filter(e=>{const b=e.getBoundingClientRect(); return b.right > innerWidth+1 || b.left < -1;}).slice(0,12).map(e=>e.className+'|'+Math.round(e.getBoundingClientRect().left)+','+Math.round(e.getBoundingClientRect().right));
  const pre=document.createElement('pre'); pre.id='probe'; pre.textContent=JSON.stringify(out,null,1); document.body.appendChild(pre);
 }, 300);
});
```
Then --dump-dom prints the whole DOM; I'll grep the JSON with python. Simpler: instead of DOM dump, I can output into document.title and use --dump-dom | grep? Let's just dump-dom and extract the <pre> content with python regex.

Note: --dump-dom with --virtual-time-budget should include the appended pre.

